      "node_id": "kg_doc_10",
      "node_type": "kg",
      "content": "Robin Goldstein is an American author, food and wine critic, and economics pundit. He is known for his books and articles questioning conventional wisdom and pricing in the food and wine industries, particularly a widely publicized exposé of Wine Spectator magazine, and for his writing on the Freakonomics blog. He is author of several books, including \"The Wine Trials\" (the world's bestselling guide to cheap wine), \"The Beer Trials\", and an upcoming book tentatively entitled \"A Defense of Fast Food\". Goldstein was also one of the subjects of \"Think Like a Freak\", the 2014 book by \"Freakonomics\" authors Steven Levitt and Stephen Dubner. He lives in Oakland, California.",
